{"number": 59, "text": "          25           Train      in   the    rain\n                       Consonant            groups        at   the     beginning           of   words\n\n                       Some  words have one consonant  sound at the beginning. Listen.\n                       late\n                       ram\n                       white  —  (wh is 2 letters but only 1 sound)\n                       Some  words have groups of two or three consonant sounds at the beginning. Listen and repeat\n                       these words. Be careful — don’t put a vowel sound between the consonants.\n                  875  Two  consonant sounds at the beginning:\n                       plate\n                       train\n                       quite     (qu is pronounced /kw/)\n                       Three consonant sounds  at the beginning:\n                       spring\n                       street\n                       square    (squ is pronounced /skw/)\n\n                       Here are some more  examples. Listen and repeat.\n                        1 bread              Pass me  some bread.\n                        2  price             What's  the price?\n                        3 bless              (sneeze) Bless you!\n                        4  class             How   many  are there in your class?\n                        5 glass              Where  are my glasses?\n                        6  cream             Do  you like ice cream?\n                        7  quiet             Isn’t it quiet?\n                        8  spell             How   do you spell it?\n                        9  stand             Where  shall I stand?\n                       10  swim              Can  you swim?\n                       11  stranger          I’m a stranger here.\n                       12  stress            a job with a lot of stress\n\n\n              58          English Pronunciation in Use (Elementary)", "char_count": 1889, "mean_conf": 90.61, "word_count